# Voxnix eval configuration
# Copy to .env.eval and fill in real values. This file is gitignored.
#
# Evals have two LLM roles:
#   1. Agent-under-test — the Voxnix agent running against a real model
#   2. Judge model — deepeval's gpt-4.1 scoring the agent's output
#
# The simplest setup: set OPENROUTER_API_KEY below. That single key
# authenticates both the test model (default: Haiku 4.5 via OpenRouter)
# and the judge (gpt-4.1 via OpenRouter's OpenAI-compatible endpoint).
#
# Non-LLM settings (VOXNIX_FLAKE_PATH, TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, etc.) are
# injected automatically by the _mock_settings fixture — no need to set them.

# ── API key ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set at least one. This key must cover both the test model's provider
# and the judge (which uses the OpenAI client internally).
#
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY is the easiest option — one key covers both roles.
# conftest aliases it to OPENAI_API_KEY and sets OPENAI_BASE_URL so the
# judge routes through OpenRouter's OpenAI-compatible endpoint.
#
# OPENAI_API_KEY works natively for the judge. If your test model also
# uses OpenAI (LLM_PROVIDER=openai), one key covers both roles.
# If your test model uses a different provider, you'll need that
# provider's key too.

# Uncomment one:
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-your-key-here

# ── Test model (optional — sensible defaults) ──────────────────
# LLM_PROVIDER and LLM_MODEL control which single model is evaluated.
# They default to openrouter / anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5, so with
# just OPENROUTER_API_KEY set above, everything works out of the box.
#
# Override to test a different model:
# LLM_PROVIDER=openrouter
# LLM_MODEL=anthropic/claude-haiku-4.5
